-- title:
--   Uniqueness of the period value of an admissible rigidification
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, $k$ an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, and $\iota : \mathbb{W}(\mathbb{F}_{p^2}) \to \mathbb{W}(k)$ a ring homomorphism; write $\bar\iota$ for $\iota$ followed by reduction modulo the ideal generated by $p$. Let $\Phi$ be a formal $O_D$-module over $\mathbb{W}(k)/p$ which is special for $\bar\iota$ (its Lie algebra is the direct sum of the two eigen-submodules `lieZero` and `lieOne`, each invertible), of height $4$ (the kernel of multiplication by $p$ has degree $p^4$), with the degree-$0$ and degree-$1$ graded pieces of its Cartier module complementary, as witnessed by `hcΦ`; let $r_\Phi : (\mathbb{Z}_p)^2 \to N$ be an additive map into the $N$-module of the associated graded Cartier module datum which, for every canonical $L$-map $L$, is a bijection from the whole source onto the degree-$0$ $\eta$-piece of $L$. Let $B$ be a noetherian commutative $\mathbb{Z}_p$-algebra in which $p$ is nilpotent, $\psi : \mathbb{W}(k) \to B$ a ring homomorphism, and $t$ a rigidified object over $B$ which is admissible for $(\iota,\psi)$: its formal module is special, of height $4$, and $\rho$ is an isogeny of height $4n$ from $\Phi$ base-changed along $\psi$ to the reduction of $t.X$. Then any two Deligne data $d,d'$ over $B$ for $\mathbb{Q}_p$ and the uniformiser $p$, each admitting a Drinfeld datum $Q$ forming a Cartier quadruple with $t$ and having $d$ (respectively $d'$) as its Deligne datum, are equal.
--
--   This is the uniqueness half of the period map underlying the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation: an admissible rigidified special formal module has at most one associated point of Drinfeld's formal upper half plane. It is used in the construction of the period map attached to a moduli package.
-- source:
